  "executionHelpText": "Per 20 Pa.C.S. § 5822 / § 5832, a Mental Health Advance Directive must be signed on paper by you and two adult witnesses, all present at the same time. The app cannot witness it for you — this step walks you through what to do.",
  "executionFinalStepLabel": "Final step · on paper",
  "executionHeading": "Make it legal — with a pen.",
  "executionIntro": "Pennsylvania law requires a real signature on paper. We can't witness it for you — but here's exactly what to do.",
  "executionWhyNotAppLead": "Why not sign in the app? ",
  "executionWhyNotAppBody": "Under Act 194 the directive is only valid when you and two adult witnesses sign the ",
  "executionSamePaperDocument": "same paper document",
  "executionWhyNotAppTail": ", together. A tap-to-sign wouldn't hold up.",
  "executionAnyFormValid": "You don’t have to use a specific form. Pennsylvania’s official forms are recommended, not required — what makes your directive valid is its content and being signed and witnessed correctly. If a facility hands you a different form, this one still counts.",
  "executionStep1Title": "Print the packet",
  "executionStep1Body": "Print the PDF we just made. It already has signature lines for you and two witnesses.",
  "executionStep2Title": "Gather two adult witnesses",
  "executionStep2Body": "Both must be 18 or older and in the room with you when you sign. (Who can’t witness is below.)",
  "executionStep3Title": "Everyone signs, same place, same time",
  "executionStep3Body": "Sign and date the witness page in front of both witnesses. They sign right after you, while you watch.",
  "executionWitnessLead": "A witness ",
  "executionWitnessCannot": "cannot",
  "executionWitnessRest": " be your agent or alternate agent, your mental health care provider, or an employee of the facility where you receive treatment — unless they are related to you by blood, marriage, or adoption.",
